  "finding": "a latent (unobserved) confounder Z->A, Z->B makes the observational skeleton propose a SPURIOUS A-B edge. Safety holds iff the system never CONFIDENTLY asserts it: when A is intervenable, do(A) does NOT move B -> the spurious edge is REFUTED by the world (like \u00a722 Akt!->Erk); when A is NOT intervenable, the edge is UNIDENTIFIABLE and the gate flags it UNVERIFIED (abstain). Either way it never drives a confident assertion -> the never-confidently-wrong invariant EXTENDS to latent confounding. If any spurious edge were VERIFIED, that would be an honest safety breach. Toy scale; ground-truth confound."
